    "https://info.jazzhr.com/job-seekers.html": {
      "title": "Trying to apply for a job?",
      "description": "For Job Seekers | JazzHR Sign In Products Compare Resources Company Request Demo Pricing Trying to apply for a job? Please read before you proceed JazzHR is an applicant tracking system (ATS) – software that businesses use to organize their hiring process and host their career pages. JazzHR is not a job board and, unfortunately, cannot help you get a job. Please navigate back to the website where you originally tried to apply for a job and try again. If you end up back here, please reach out to the organization you’re interested in working for directly. If you are looking for a job currently, most of our customers post their open roles on all major job boards like Indeed, LinkedIn, ZipRecruiter, and more. Please go directly to those sites to search for additional open roles. (And best of luck!) If you are a business looking to evaluate recruiting software for your hiring needs, please navigate to our main website to schedule time with one of our solutions consultants. What is an applicant tracking system (ATS)? Many companies that do any kind of hiring tend to use software like JazzHR to automate the recruiting process. Read up on what an applicant tracking system is. Make sure your resume is ATS-friendly Now that you know what an ATS is, check out our blog for formatting tips and tricks to help make your application stand out. 20 Interview Tips to Make a Great Impression Ready to nail that interview? Make sure you read up on Indeed’s latest article which outlines 20 ways to make a great impression during your interviews. Looking for additional job seeker resources? Check out Indeed’s Career Guide center. Go to Indeed Products JazzHR: Foundational Hiring Lever: Scalable Hiring Jobvite: Sophisticated Hiring Applicant Tracking Candidate Texting Explore Request a Demo Pricing Events Webinars Blog Resources Marketplace Compare & Choose JazzHR vs. Greenhouse JazzHR vs. Workable Customer Stories Company About Employ Careers Contact Us Press & Media Support Help Center Employ HireEd Academy FAQ Integrations Security Privacy Policy Terms of Service Connect with Us LinkedIn © 2026 Employ Inc. All rights reserved."
    },
    "https://www.northcentral.edu/about/employment/current-job-openings/": {
      "title": "Current Job Openings",
      "description": "Jobs at NCU | Employment Minnesota Skip to content What to Study Program Finder Academic Catalog Faculty Directory Academic Success Admissions Undergraduate Students Graduate Students Transfer Students Pathways Students PSEO Students International Students NCU Parents Admitted Students After NCU Cost & Aid Tuition and Fees Types of Aid Policies & Procedures Student Account Life at NCU Spiritual Life Residence Life Minneapolis Recreation and Wellness Service Opportunities Organizations Cafeteria Campus Store Bookstore Library Safety Athletics About Mission, History, Facts Policies President Give Events Accreditations Strategic Plan Contact Emergency Management Map and Directions Campus Services Directory Alumni Employment Pastors and Churches What to Study Admissions Cost & Aid Life at NCU Athletics About Search Request Info Apply Now What to Study Program Finder Academic Catalog Faculty Directory Academic Success Admissions Undergraduate Students Graduate Students Transfer Students Pathways Students PSEO Students International Students NCU Parents Admitted Students After NCU Visit Our Campus Experience NCU in Real Life. Learn More Cost & Aid Tuition and Fees Types of Aid Policies & Procedures Student Account Life at NCU Spiritual Life Residence Life Minneapolis Recreation and Wellness Service Opportunities Organizations Campus Store Bookstore Library Cafeteria Safety Visit Our Campus Experience NCU in Real Life. Learn More About Mission, History, Facts Policies President Give Events Accreditations Strategic Plan Contact Emergency Management Map and Directions Campus Services Directory Alumni Employment Pastors and Churches Giving at NCU Explore Opportunities to Support NCU. Learn More Current Job Openings Customized Benefits Package At North Central University we value our employees and know the importance of good benefits for both the employee and their family. Therefore, we have created a competitive and comprehensive benefits package for all full-time faculty (.75) and full time staff at the University. This includes: Health insurance Dental plan Voluntary life/AD&D insurance Short-term disability insurance Long-term disability insurance Section 125 Cafeteria/Flexible Spending plan 403(b) retirement plan 20% off at the Campus Store Free parking and more (how about all-you-can eat “3 dollar days” in our cafeteria) NCU Benefits Summary Tuition Benefit Employee Tuition Benefit Regular full-time (40 hours per week) and regular part-time with benefit employees (30+ hours per week) are permitted and encouraged to take up to three North Central credits in the fall and spring semesters. The employee tuition benefit discount does not extend to summer course offerings. With the tuition benefit discount, tuition, general fees and technology fees are waived. Applied lesson, directed research, and class fees are the responsibility of the employee. Employee Dependent Tuition Benefit Discount The spouse and/or dependent children (as defined by federal financial aid regulations) of regular full-time (40 hours per week) employees may receive up to 100% paid tuition through the Employee Dependent Tuition Benefit Discount. The Employee Dependent Tuition Benefit Discount can only be applied to tuition. All other costs such as general fees, class fees, housing, textbooks and meal plans are the responsibility of the student (whether the student is full-time status or part-time status). In order to qualify for the Employee Dependent Tuition Benefit Discount, all spouses/dependents who are taking 6 or more credits MUST first file for federal and state financial aid. Paid Time Off Vacation North Central University provides a flexible Paid Time Off (PTO) Program for the purpose of providing All regular full-time employees and permanent part-time employees with the opportunity to take time away from work without loss of compensation. The PTO Program is an inclusive time off program intended for use in connection with vacations, short-term injuries, and illnesses (non-work related) of five (5) days or less, personal business, family care, and other needs that may require time off from work. Discretionary Leave Full-time regular employees are awarded a total of 48 hours (6 days) of discretionary leave per calendar year. This is available for sickness, medical appointments, personal time, etc. Holiday Pay NCU currently has 10 paid holidays that are observed as paid-time-off for employees. In addition to these holidays, Christmas week is also observed as paid-time-off when granted by the President’s Cabinet (this is voted upon annually and not guaranteed on an annual basis). Sign Up for Our Newsletter 910 Elliot Ave. Minneapolis, Minnesota, 55404 t: 800.289.6222 f: 612.343.4778 Quick Links What to Study Admissions About Us Visit Our Campus Give Employment Explore Life at NCU Athletics Program Finder Events Rental Spaces Alumni Support Tuition & Aid Blog Career Services Contact Us After NCU Transcripts Campus Services Legal Terms of Service Policy Title IX Policy Anti Hazing and Bias Policy Consumer Information About Us Cookies Policy © 2026 North Central University. All rights reserved."
    },
    "https://www.northcentral.edu/alumni/career-services/": {
      "title": "Career Services",
      "description": "Career Services at North Central University | NCU Alumni Support Skip to content What to Study Program Finder Academic Catalog Faculty Directory Academic Success Admissions Undergraduate Students Graduate Students Transfer Students Pathways Students PSEO Students International Students NCU Parents Admitted Students After NCU Cost & Aid Tuition and Fees Types of Aid Policies & Procedures Student Account Life at NCU Spiritual Life Residence Life Minneapolis Recreation and Wellness Service Opportunities Organizations Cafeteria Campus Store Bookstore Library Safety Athletics About Mission, History, Facts Policies President Give Events Accreditations Strategic Plan Contact Emergency Management Map and Directions Campus Services Directory Alumni Employment Pastors and Churches What to Study Admissions Cost & Aid Life at NCU Athletics About Search Request Info Apply Now What to Study Program Finder Academic Catalog Faculty Directory Academic Success Admissions Undergraduate Students Graduate Students Transfer Students Pathways Students PSEO Students International Students NCU Parents Admitted Students After NCU Visit Our Campus Experience NCU in Real Life. Learn More Cost & Aid Tuition and Fees Types of Aid Policies & Procedures Student Account Life at NCU Spiritual Life Residence Life Minneapolis Recreation and Wellness Service Opportunities Organizations Campus Store Bookstore Library Cafeteria Safety Visit Our Campus Experience NCU in Real Life. Learn More About Mission, History, Facts Policies President Give Events Accreditations Strategic Plan Contact Emergency Management Map and Directions Campus Services Directory Alumni Employment Pastors and Churches Giving at NCU Explore Opportunities to Support NCU. Learn More Career Services Explore your calling and career paths with support from NCU. Support to Advance in Your Career At North Central University, we’re committed to providing career-relevant, Christ-centered education so that you’re ready to engage in servant leadership and pursue your calling in a successful career. Whether you graduated years ago, are taking a break from your education, or plan to graduate soon, Career Services offers tips and tools designed to help you advance your career or step into a new career with confidence. Through Career Services, you can: Connect with our alumni network Browse local job listings and our career library Get a fresh headshot at one of our events Prepare for a job interview Explore local internship opportunities and request references Fine tune your resume Meet with a career advisor to match your callings with career paths Get tips for applying, requesting references, interview follow-up, and more Explore the resources below to get started. Build Your Professional Network Facebook Affinity Groups: North Central University Alumni North Central University Alumni in Business NCU Biblical Studies Society Continue Your Education Some career paths require graduate-level training or degrees. Our career services team can help you discern whether furthering your education will help you meet requirements and gain marketable skills for your vocation. NCU alumni can receive 25% discount on tuition for select graduate programs: Master of Arts in Strategic Leadership Master of Arts in Biblical Theology Explore NCU Job Listings We welcome NCU alumni to check the employment opportunities at NCU and apply to join our team. NCU Employment Members of the NCU community regularly share their job postings with Career Services when they are seeking to fill a position or internship. Visit this page regularly for new listings. Contact Hannah Sawczak at hnsawcza@northcentral.edu if you have an opportunity to post for our alumni. Students and alumni can join the North Central University Current Students & Alumni group on LinkedIn. It’s a dedicated space to connect, network, and share internship, fellowship, and job opportunities. The group is designed to support the personal and professional growth of NCU students and alumni by helping them build meaningful connections and access valuable career resources. NCU Job Board Contact Career Services We’re here for you! Email Hannah Sawczak at hnsawcza@northcentral.edu with your questions about career services, opportunities, or events. Sign Up for Our Newsletter 910 Elliot Ave. Minneapolis, Minnesota, 55404 t: 800.289.6222 f: 612.343.4778 Quick Links What to Study Admissions About Us Visit Our Campus Give Employment Explore Life at NCU Athletics Program Finder Events Rental Spaces Alumni Support Tuition & Aid Blog Career Services Contact Us After NCU Transcripts Campus Services Legal Terms of Service Policy Title IX Policy Anti Hazing and Bias Policy Consumer Information About Us Cookies Policy © 2026 North Central University. All rights reserved."
    }
  },
